  abstract = {A study addressed the challenges of feature extraction and model training efficiency in speaker recognition by introducing a novel Real Additive Angular Marlin Loss function to optimize performance. In the experiment, specific neural networks were employed to extract voice and facial features, and an attention-based feature fusion approach was applied to enhance classification. The results showed that the Equal Error Rate (EER) on the SpeakingFaces dataset was reduced to 2.5%, significantly outperforming existing methods. This study not only improved the accuracy of speaker recognition but also provided new insights and methods for related research fields.},
}

